  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let $I=\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{x^{3} \\cos 3 x}{2+x^{2}} d x$. Then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gD7LF",
      "text": "$-\\frac{1}{2}    < I < \\frac{1}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9Hufq",
      "text": "$-\\frac{1}{3}    < I < \\frac{1}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Sew9C",
      "text": "$-1    < I < 1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "paJsQ",
      "text": "$-\\frac{3}{2}    < I < \\frac{3}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$I=\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{x^{3} \\cos 3 x}{2+x^{2}} d x$\r\nHere, $\\quad-1    < \\cos 3 x < 1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad-x^{3} < x^{3} \\cos 3 x < x^{3}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{-x^{3}}{x^{2}} < \\frac{-x^{3}}{x} < \\frac{-x^{3}}{2+x^{2}} < \\frac{x^{3} \\cos 3 x}{2+x^{2}}$\r\n$ < \\frac{x^{3}}{2+x^{2}} < \\frac{x^{3}}{x} < \\frac{x^{3}}{x^{2}}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\int_{0}^{1}-x^{2} d x < I < \\int_{0}^{1} x^{2} d x$\r\n$\\Rightarrow$\r\n$\\left(\\frac{-x^{3}}{3}\\right)_{0}^{1} < I < \\left(\\frac{x^{3}}{3}\\right)_{0}^{1}$\r\n$\\frac{-1}{3} < I < \\frac{1}{3}$",
    "image": null
  },
